From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:26:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: Clear takes a question of the question card back to
 unanswered
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.42 (ask 66, 2026-11-16). A single-select question is
a radio group: once an option was picked there was no way back to no
answer, and a multi-select could only be undone box by box. Each select
question now shows a Clear at the end of its title while it has an
answer. It resets the select and the question's own "Other" box -- the
companion that names it through `_askUserQuestionCustomAnswer`, the pair a
page already keeps together -- and drops their validation errors, so a
required question fails Submit again exactly as an untouched one does.

The handler is set with ElicitationCardHandlers::with_clear_selection
rather than one more constructor argument, so the card's other callers
keep compiling unchanged; unset it is a no-op. Tests in
elicitation/clear_selection_tests.rs; Red seen with clear_answers made a
no-op.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
